    createStaticVNode('<h1 id="_3-c51-example" tabindex="-1">3. C51 Example <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-c51-example" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3. C51 Example&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="_3-1-preparation" tabindex="-1">3.1 Preparation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-1-preparation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.1 Preparation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This example uses the <strong>STC15W4K16S4</strong> main control chip with an open-source servo controller expansion board. Connect the 4-ch line follower sensor to the 5V pin, GND pin, and four IO pins on the expansion board with a 6P cable.</p><img loading="lazy" height="1269" width="1200" src="' + _imports_0 + '" class="common_img" style="width:400px;"><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:center;">Pin</th><th style="text-align:center;">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:center;">5V</td><td style="text-align:center;">Power input</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">GND</td><td style="text-align:center;">Power ground</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">S1</td><td style="text-align:center;">P24</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">S2</td><td style="text-align:center;">P54</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">S3</td><td style="text-align:center;">P55</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">S4</td><td style="text-align:center;">P32</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="note custom-block github-alert"><p class="custom-block-title">NOTE</p><p></p><p><strong>The detection distance can be adjusted with the knobs, allowing the sensitivity to be tuned for different environments. For calibration, first place the infrared probes over a black area and adjust the knobs until all blue indicator lights turn on. Then slowly rotate the knobs until the lights just turn off. Next, place the probes over a white area and continue adjusting until the lights just turn on. The probes are now set to the optimal sensitivity, as shown in the figure.</strong></p></div><img loading="lazy" height="204" width="205" src="' + _imports_1 + '" class="common_img" style="width:300px;"><h2 id="_3-2-example-program" tabindex="-1">3.2 Example Program <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-2-example-program" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.2 Example Program&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The 4-ch line follower sensor operates by infrared detection. It includes four probes, and each probe contains one transmitter and one receiver.</p><ol><li><p>Connect the development board with the expansion board installed to the computer with a USB cable, or use the extended serial port.</p></li><li><p>Open the C51 example program in the <strong>Example Program</strong> folder. For program download, refer to <strong><a href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/14Vqtvup7l7_GOG_bX5j2_-xE8iwDuLqN?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2. Softwares/01 C51 Tool/Set Development Environment</a></strong>. During programming, select the correct option <img loading="lazy" height="23" width="97" src="' + _imports_2 + '" class="common_img" style="width:150px;">and use the value that matches the detected frequency.</p></li></ol><h2 id="_3-3-program-outcome" tabindex="-1">3.3 Program Outcome <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-3-program-outcome" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.3 Program Outcome&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><p>Applicable platforms include Mecanum-wheel, differential-drive, tank, and Ackermann chassis.</p></li><li><p>Prepare a sheet of white paper with a black line, or draw several black lines on white paper.</p></li><li><p>Place the sensor probes over the black line and the white background, then open the <strong>Serial Monitor</strong> in the IDE. The readings from the four probes are displayed as <code>1</code> or <code>0</code>. When a probe is over a black line, the corresponding indicator turns off, and the reading is <code>1</code>. When a probe is over a white area, the corresponding indicator turns on, and the reading is <code>0</code>. Make sure the serial port settings are correct.</p></li></ol><img loading="lazy" height="575" width="637" src="' + _imports_3 + '" class="common_img" style="width:500px;"><h2 id="_3-4-program-analysis" tabindex="-1">3.4 Program Analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-4-program-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.4 Program Analysis&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The program uses four line following channels to detect the black line and outputs the logic levels of each channel through the serial port. A reading of <code>1</code> indicates that the corresponding probe is over a black line. A reading of <code>0</code> indicates that the corresponding probe is over a white area. The program is shown in the figure below.</p><img loading="lazy" height="72" width="674" src="' + _imports_4 + '" class="common_img" style="width:600px;"><img loading="lazy" height="709" width="749" src="' + _imports_5 + '" class="common_img" style="width:600px;">', 17)
